      "pins": ["U1.8", "R5.1", "R5.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "U1 pin 8 (EN/CHIP_PU) is connected to the GND net. R5 is connected between +3V3 and GND (pin 2 to +3V3, pin 1 to GND).",
      "expected": "U1 pin 8 (EN/CHIP_PU) should be pulled up to +3V3, typically via a 10k resistor (R5), to enable the ESP32-C3. R5 should be between +3V3 and U1.8, not between +3V3 and GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"EN/CHIP_PU\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R5\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R5\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "pull-up/pull-down resistors R2/R5/R6/R11 (strapping/EN/fan-tach related)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The ESP32-C3 EN pin is held low, keeping the MCU in reset. The board will not boot or run firmware.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C7"],
      "pins": ["C7.1", "C7.2"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "C7 (10uF) has both pin 1 and pin 2 connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "C7 should be a decoupling capacitor between +3V3 and GND, with one pin on +3V3 and the other on GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C7\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C7\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C7 0 0 10u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "C7 provides no decoupling; the +3V3 rail lacks this 10uF bulk capacitance, potentially causing instability or noise on the 3.3V supply.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain two anomalies: the ESP32-C3 EN pin (U1.8) is tied to GND instead of being pulled up to +3V3 via R5, which will hold the MCU in reset; and C7 (10uF) has both terminals on GND, so it provides no decoupling for the +3V3 rail."
}

